{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And the sense of <b>If Your face does not go</b> according to Rashi's opinion is: this is what I desire, for by the hand of an angel do not bring us up from here. And it would be unthinkable that he should say 'If Your face does not go' after He had already promised him 'My face will go.' And Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] explained (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 33:21) that HaShem said to Moses: I Myself will go, and I will grant rest to you alone, for with you alone will I go; and Moses responded: If Your face does not go with the entire nation, do not bring us up from here — and therefore he said 'תעלנו' in the plural. This too is not satisfactory, for Moses first said 'You have not made known to me whom You will send with me' in the singular, and behold, even at the time of favor before the sin, He said <b>Behold, I send an angel before you to guard you and to bring you</b>; and if He were speaking to Israel, He would say this too on their account. Furthermore, if so, Moses would be asking that He make known to him which angel He would send with him — but behold, he wanted the angel of whom it is said (Exodus 23:21) 'for My name is within him,' and HaShem answered him with a twofold and redoubled goodness, more than what he asked — that He Himself would go.\\n\\nBut this passage cannot be grasped by one who has not heard the secrets of the Torah, and thus is the matter by way of truth: Moses said <b>And You have not made known to me</b> which angel You will send with me, and he sought that He fulfill for him two things that He had said to him. The first: <b>I have known you by name</b> — that is, that I be known by My name for your sake; and it is possible that 'And You' said this from what He had said to him, 'and My name YHWH I did not make known to them' (Exodus 6:3), as I have explained (see beginning of Va'era). And the second thing: <b>and you have found favor in My eyes</b> — that he find favor, and this is the adhesion of thought. And he said <b>And now, if I have found favor in Your eyes</b> — in the attribute of justice — <b>make known to me, I pray</b> the pathways of the ways as You are known by Your name; <b>and I will know You</b> — to unify You, in order that I find the great favor; <b>and see that this nation is Your people</b> — You are their father and they are Your children. And to this Onkelos intends when he says: 'Make known to me now Your good path, and let me know Your compassion.' Then the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: <b>My face will go</b> — the angel of the covenant, whom you desire that through him My face be seen, concerning whom it is said 'In a time of favor I answered you' (Isaiah 49:8), for My name is within him; <b>and I will grant rest</b> — him — <b>to you</b> — that I will not conduct Myself with you in the fierce attribute of justice, but in an attribute included within the attribute of mercy, from the language of 'And it shall be when YHWH your Elohim grants you rest from all your enemies' (Deuteronomy 25:19); and it is like the matter that is said (Ezekiel 5:13) 'Thus My anger shall be spent, and I will cause My wrath to rest upon them.' Then Moses answered: <b>If Your face</b> — in Your very self and in Your glory — <b>does not go</b>, <b>do not bring us up from here</b> — that You be with us face to face, for so were the conditions in the portion of Va'era (above 6:6–8), and so he mentioned above (Exodus 32:11) 'with great power and with a strong hand,' and behold, he asks that He bring them up to the land with great power and with a strong hand as He brought them out of Egypt with them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "Where Ramban writes והנחותי אותו לך, the word 'him' (אותו) refers back to 'the angel of the covenant' just mentioned; the syntax is strained and is translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:03.755657266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}